\section{Executive Summary}
%===========================================================

The ASCE-HPC-V4 platform is an exascale-class high-performance computing 
architecture engineered for real-time atmospheric physics simulation, 
post-quantum cryptographic execution, and high-throughput tensor computation. 
The system integrates multi-GPU compute blades, high-bandwidth memory, 
Dragonfly interconnect topology, direct-to-chip two-phase cooling, 
and a 54\,V DC busbar power envelope optimized for 400\,kW cabinet loads.

The platform is designed for:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Real-time physical atmospheric modeling
    \item Post-quantum lattice cryptography (Kyber-1024, Dilithium5)
    \item Tensor-heavy workloads (HBM3e, mesh interconnect)
    \item Multi-petabyte parallel file system throughput
\end{itemize}

